# This CITATION.cff file was generated for the Zenodo deposit of the
# analysis code and data of the manuscript:
#   "Urgent and balanced action needed to achieve global biodiversity framework"
# After the deposit is published, add the Zenodo DOI to the "doi:" field below
# and the manuscript DOI to "preferred-citation" (see ZENODO_UPLOAD.md).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code and data, please cite this repository and the associated manuscript."
type: software
title: "Code and data for: Urgent and balanced action needed to achieve global biodiversity framework"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Complete analysis code and all data needed to reproduce the results of the
  manuscript "Urgent and balanced action needed to achieve global biodiversity
  framework", which quantifies national progress towards the 23 targets and
  4 goals of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework (GBF). The
  repository contains the computation pipeline (indicator harmonization and
  imputation, normalization, target and goal aggregation, the Mean and Evenness
  Index Scores, synergy and country contributions, projected growth rates,
  achievement rates and the four-class trajectory classification), the derived
  analyses behind the Supplementary Tables and Figures, the raw indicator data
  and metadata, the intermediate checkpoints, and the figure and table source
  data. All paths in the scripts are relative to the repository root;
  RUN_GUIDE.md describes the exact run order and the conventions of every
  input file. The code is written in R (developed with R 4.5.3).
keywords:
  - Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework
  - GBF
  - biodiversity
  - conservation targets
  - indicators
  - achievement rate
  - projection
  - reproducibility
